Building a Raspberry Pi Robot by Hand: A Step-by-Step Guide

To create a robot using a Raspberry Pi and Arduino, you'll need a few components. In this tutorial, we'll use the Adafruit Huzzah library to connect the Raspberry Pi to the Arduino and create a robot that can read temperature, humidity, and light levels.

First, connect the Arduino Uno to your computer using a Micro-USB cable. Then, connect the Adafruit Huzzah board to the Arduino using the provided jumper wires. The Huzzah library will read the temperature and humidity data from the sensors and send it to the Raspberry Pi.

Next, you'll need to create a robot frame to house the Raspberry Pi and Arduino boards. You can use a piece of wood or a 3D printed frame. For this tutorial, we'll use a simple wooden frame.

Once you have your robot frame built, you'll need to connect the sensors to the Arduino board. The Adafruit Huzzah library will read the data from the sensors and send it to the Raspberry Pi.

Here is the Arduino code used in this tutorial:

```cpp
